    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the repository's single test class \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` with both the new soft-delete cases \u2014 passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed owner deletion from a hard delete to a soft delete. Changes made:\n\n**Domain / persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`, defaults to `false`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)`.\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a `deleted` column defaulting to `FALSE NOT NULL`. (Tests run under the `hsqldb` profile, whose grammar requires `DEFAULT` before `NOT NULL`; h2 uses the same order, mysql/postgres use their conventional order.)\n\n**API contract / mapping**\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and GET responses include it. MapStruct auto-maps it from the entity.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"deleted\", ignore = true)` to `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` so a newly created owner keeps its `false` default.\n\n**Controller (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)**\n- `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true` and saves (returning 204) instead of removing the row.\n- `requireUniqueIdentity` and `requireHouseholdNotDuplicate` now filter out soft-deleted owners, so a normally-blocking duplicate/identity match is allowed when the only matching owner has been deleted. Updated their Javadocs accordingly.\n\nBehavior now matches the spec: DELETE flags the owner deleted and retains the record (2xx); GET still returns it with `deleted: true`; a newly created owner has `deleted: false`; and the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners.",
